 \, 'script'\, 'qgiv-embedjs')\; Have you ever been interested in joining C
 ool Petaluma's block-based Cool Teams program but faced barriers to implem
 enting it in your neighborhood?&nbsp\; Thanks to the support of our two Am
 eriCorps fellows\, Auggie and Raelyn\, Cool Petaluma will be offering a mo
 nthly Cool Teams program open to anyone interested in turning climate conc
 ern into collective action! Beginning on March 25th\, sessions will be hel
 d from 6 pm to 7:30 pm on the last Wednesday of each month. This month's s
 ession will be held alongside our gorgeous Petaluma Slough at the barn at 
 Steamer Landing Park. If you've been unable to implement our program in th
 e past due to HOA&nbsp\;restrictions\, difficult neighborhood locations\, 
 lack of time\, or the demands of leadership\, now is your chance to partic
 ipate. Don't miss out on this special opportunity to connect with like-min
 ded neighbors! All attendees will receive their very own FREE Personal Eme
 rgency Preparedness Plan\, courtesy of the County. #block-c3c807ec3963152d
